From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pletch <17855860+pletch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:44:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dummynet_st: a vnet going away turns packets off first

The thirteenth of the sub-tick release series (opnsense-cake SUBTICK.md),
from a source review.

ip_dn_vnet_destroy() frees the packets staged for the vnet (patch 0008)
and then destroys its lock, on the word that ip_dn_destroy() had waited
for dummynet_io(). That holds when the module is unloaded; when a jail
with its own vnet is removed nothing had waited, so a packet still in
dummynet_io() could be staged after the list was emptied, and leak, or
(as in the stock dummynet) take the lock as it was destroyed.

Now the vnet's init_done is cleared first, under the lock, and
dummynet_io() frees a packet for a vnet without it; then the network
epoch is waited for, which packets in dummynet_io() are in, before the
flush. dummynet's tasks already pass over a vnet without init_done.
---
 sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_io.c    |  6 ++++++
 sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dummynet.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_io.c b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_io.c
index c1bbb40..42ef6c3 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_io.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_io.c
@@ -1327,6 +1327,12 @@ dummynet_io(struct mbuf **m0, struct ip_fw_args *fwa)
 		dir |= PROTO_LAYER2;
 	else if (fwa->flags & IPFW_ARGS_IP6)
 		dir |= PROTO_IPV6;
+	/* the vnet is going away (ip_dn_vnet_destroy()), its lock with it */
+	if (__predict_false(!V_dn_cfg.init_done)) {
+		FREE_PKT(m);
+		*m0 = NULL;
+		return (ENOBUFS);
+	}
 	/* tag outside the lock: m_tag_get() allocates */
 	if (tag_mbuf(m, dir, fwa)) {
 		DN_BH_WLOCK();
diff --git a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dummynet.c b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dummynet.c
index 0d23f88..b7b3d91 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dummynet.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dummynet.c
@@ -2667,9 +2667,21 @@ ip_dn_vnet_destroy(void)
 {
 	struct mbuf *m, *next;
 
+	/*
+	 * Turn packets away from this vnet's dummynet (dummynet_io() checks
+	 * init_done) and wait for those already in it. On unload
+	 * ip_dn_destroy() has done as much for every vnet; when a jail goes
+	 * away nothing had, and a packet could be staged after the list was
+	 * emptied below, or meet the lock destroyed.
+	 */
+	DN_BH_WLOCK();
+	V_dn_cfg.init_done = 0;
+	DN_BH_WUNLOCK();
+	NET_EPOCH_WAIT();
+
 	DN_BH_WLOCK();
 	dummynet_flush();
-	/* nothing stages any more (ip_dn_destroy() waited for dummynet_io()) */
+	/* nothing stages any more */
 	for (m = V_dn_cfg.staged; m != NULL; m = next) {
 		next = m->m_nextpkt;
 		m->m_nextpkt = NULL;
